==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cat Kart G''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Cat Kart P''' when obtained from [[Cat Kart Awakens!]] (may be dropped on the first stage but guaranteed on the second stage) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit has literally no usage whatsoever. [[Thief Cat (Rare Cat)|Thief Cat]] outclasses this unit in every single way: attack speed, cooldown, and stats. In addition to that, Thief Cat's [[True Form]], Goemon, has Area Attack, something that Cat Kart pitifully attempts to replicate with its pathetic excuse of a Multi-Hit.  Assuming your luck is bad enough to somehow never get Thief Cat or [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], you can always resort to using low-tier letdowns such as [[Reindeer Fish Cat (Rare Cat)|Reindeer Fish Cat]], [[Maneki Cat (Special Cat)|Maneki Cat]], or even [[Farmer Cat (Special Cat)|Farmer Cat]] due to all three having stats that are better than Cat Kart's. While Cat Kart's 320 range at first seems appealing due to this being the highest range out of any spammble Double Bounty unit, this actually does not change anything regarding its viability. Cat Kart has the health of a pickle, meaning its range advantage will not help it out much due to Cat Kart still being extremely vulnerable to any forms of piercing attacks, such as Surges, Waves, or Long Distance attacks. 320 range is also very poor, with most standard backliners like Teacher Bear or Le'Boin being able to outrange and kill Cat Kart. A stack of Cat Karts is very hard to accomplish due to its lengthy cooldown, and even once built, a stack of Cat Karts still does not deal a significant amount of damage; you'll be hardpressed to find any standard peon past early SoL which Cat Kart can score Double Bounty kills on. Even in the [[Underground Labyrinth]], Cat Kart's cooldown and stats are ill-suited for clearing out peons, and its range leaves it vulnerable to many an enemy.

Overall, Cat Kart R is a unit with many cons and little pros to speak of, and you should not bother with using it in your lineup, as it will almost certainly be a waste of a slot. 

