==Trivia==
*Cat Kart R is a reference to the [[mariowiki:Mario Kart (series)|Mario Kart]] series.
**Cat Kart R is based on Mario, with the R standing for Red.
***Cat Kart R's hobbies mentioned in its description are references to various spin-offs of the Mario series, parties for the [[mariowiki:Mario Party (series)|Mario Party]] series, tennis for the [[mariowiki:Mario Tennis (series)|Mario Tennis]] series and medicine for the [[mariowiki:Dr. Mario (series)|Dr. Mario]] series.
**Cat Kart G is based on Luigi (being slightly taller and a different color), with the G standing for Green.
***Cat Kart G's description references how Luigi is depicted as being in Mario's shadow as the less popular brother.
**Cat Kart P is based on Peach, with hair, crown and Mario-Kart-specific ponytail. The P in her name stands for Pink.
***Cat Kart P's description references the quote "But Our Princess is in Another Castle!" from the Toads at the end of the first seven worlds of the original ''[[mariowiki:Super Mario Bros.|Super Mario Bros.]]'', which became a meme on the internet due to its infamy.
***Additionally, the three cans of [[Cat Food]] behind her reference the [[mariowiki:Triple Bananas|Triple Bananas]] item, originally from Mario Kart Arcade GP.
*Although Cat Kart R was made to promote [[The Battle Cats POP!]], it does not appear in said game.
*Cat Kart R is the only Cat Unit to use [[Cat Food]] as a weapon.
*The [[Enemy Bases|Enemy Base]] Cat Kart R appears on is altered to resemble the [[mariowiki:Fortress|fortresses]] that appear after beating a stage in ''Super Mario Bros.''.

